This tool's suite cannot be a test/run.sh, so self-test.yml's discovery skips it.

Covered instead by these named jobs in .github/workflows/self-test.yml:

  betterleaks-self-scan       dogfoods the action against this repo (uses:)
  betterleaks-pinned-version  asserts the step OUTPUT version == v1.8.0 (uses:)
  betterleaks-shellcheck      yq-extracts every run: block and ShellChecks it

The first two assert behavior that exists only through `uses:`, and a step output
has no meaning outside it. A discovered shell script cannot express either.

Deleting this file makes the tools matrix demand a test/run.sh again, which is the
intended behavior for every tool that does not have this exemption in writing.
